# Production Architecture: High-Throughput MVCC In-Memory Key-Value Index with Lock-Free SkipList, EBR, and `io_uring` Group-Commit WAL

---

## 1. Architecture & Formal Memory Model Rationale

```
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                     Application Worker Threads                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
       |                                      |                                       |
       | 1. Read at ReadTS                    | 2. Point Update (CAS)                 | 3. Submit WAL Request
       v                                      v                                       v
+-----------------------+           +-----------------------+               +-----------------------+
|  Lock-Free Traversal  |           |   MVCC Version Chain  |               |    Lock-Free MPSC     |
|   (Wait-Free Reads)   |           |   (Prepends Latest)   |               |     Request Queue     |
+-----------------------+           +-----------------------+               +-----------------------+
       |                                      |                                       |
       | Uses Tagged Pointers                 | Safe Memory Retirement                | Batched Aggregation
       v                                      v                                       v
+-----------------------------------------------------------+               +-----------------------+
|             Lock-Free Multi-Level SkipList                |               | Dedicated WAL Worker  |
|            (Harris-Sundell Node Splice/Unlink)            |               |  (Linux io_uring)     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+               +-----------------------+
                              |                                                       |
                              v                                                       v
            +------------------------------------+                  +-----------------------------------+
            |     3-Epoch Memory Reclamation     |                  |  Group Commit Fixed 4KB Buffers   |
            |   (Quiescent Barrier / Safe Free)  |                  | (IORING_OP_WRITE_FIXED + FSYNC)   |
            +------------------------------------+                  +-----------------------------------+
```

### 1.1 Memory Ordering & Synchronization Proofs

The storage engine is engineered around fine-grained C++20 atomic operations. Sequential consistency (`std::memory_order_seq_cst`) introduces full bidirectional store-load memory barriers (`mfence` or `dmb ish`) that drain CPU store buffers, severely degrading multi-socket scaling. We replace this with explicit **Acquire-Release** synchronization:

1. **Forward Pointer Traversal (`std::memory_order_acquire`)**:
   - When a reader traverses a forward pointer `curr->next[i].load(std::memory_order_acquire)`, the acquire semantic synchronizes with the `std::memory_order_release` store of the thread that inserted or spliced `curr->next[i]`.
   - **Invariant**: Any memory written to `curr` (including its key, tower height, and MVCC version head) prior to publication is guaranteed to be visible to the traversing reader.

2. **Marked Pointer Deletion (Harris-Sundell Protocol)**:
   - A node is deleted in two phases:
     - **Logical Deletion**: The lowest bit (LSB) of `curr->next[i]` is atomically tagged (`MARK_BIT = 0x1`) using CAS with `std::memory_order_acq_rel`. If a thread attempts to insert after `curr` while `curr` is being marked, the CAS fails, preventing dangling links.
     - **Physical Unlink**: Splicing the predecessor's pointer (`pred->next[i].compare_exchange_weak(curr, succ, std::memory_order_acq_rel, std::memory_order_acquire)`) unlinks the logically marked node.

3. **MVCC Version Chain Invariant**:
   - Each index node stores an atomic pointer `head_version` pointing to a singly linked list of versions sorted by `commit_ts` descending:
     $$V_{\text{newest}} \to V_{\text{older}} \to \dots \to V_{\text{oldest}}$$
   - Prepending a new version $V_{\text{new}}$ performs `V_new->next.store(old_head, std::memory_order_relaxed)` followed by `head_version.compare_exchange_weak(old_head, V_new, std::memory_order_release, std::memory_order_relaxed)`.
   - A reader performing `head_version.load(std::memory_order_acquire)` establishes a happens-before relationship, guaranteeing that all fields of $V_{\text{new}}$ (value buffer, commit timestamp, tombstone flag) are visible without data races.

4. **Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR) Correctness**:
   - Global epoch $E \in \{0, 1, 2\}$. A thread enters an epoch critical section by reading $E$ and publishing its local active epoch via `local_epoch.store(E, std::memory_order_release)`.
   - An epoch $E$ can advance to $(E + 1) \bmod 3$ if and only if **no active thread** has `local_epoch == (E - 1) \bmod 3`.
   - Any memory retired during epoch $E_{\text{retire}}$ is guaranteed to have no active pointer references once all threads have progressed past $E_{\text{retire}}$. It is safely deallocated when the global epoch reaches $(E_{\text{retire}} + 2) \bmod 3$.

---

## 2. Complete C++20 Implementation

### 2.1 Dependencies and Core Definitions

```cpp
#ifndef MVCC_STORAGE_ENGINE_HPP
#define MVCC_STORAGE_ENGINE_HPP

#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <string>
#include <string_view>
#include <memory>
#include <atomic>
#include <thread>
#include <chrono>
#include <cstring>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cassert>
#include <random>
#include <array>
#include <functional>
#include <optional>
#include <fcntl.h>
#include <unistd.h>
#include <sys/stat.h>
#include <sys/types.h>
#include <sys/uio.h>
#include <linux/fs.h>
#include <liburing.h>
#include <x86intrin.h> // SSE4.2 CRC32 (with fallback)

namespace mvcc {

// ============================================================================
// 1. Hardware-Accelerated CRC32C
// ============================================================================
inline uint32_t calculate_crc32c(uint32_t crc, const uint8_t* data, size_t length) {
#if defined(__SSE4_2__) && defined(__x86_64__)
    size_t i = 0;
    while (i + 8 <= length) {
        crc = static_cast<uint32_t>(_mm_crc32_u64(crc, *reinterpret_cast<const uint64_t*>(data + i)));
        i += 8;
    }
    if (i + 4 <= length) {
        crc = _mm_crc32_u32(crc, *reinterpret_cast<const uint32_t*>(data + i));
        i += 4;
    }
    while (i < length) {
        crc = _mm_crc32_u8(crc, data[i]);
        i++;
    }
    return crc;
#else
    // Software CRC32C fallback
    static const uint32_t table[256] = {
        0x00000000, 0xF26B8303, 0xE13B70F7, 0x1350F3F4, 0xC79A971F, 0x35F1141C, 0x26A1E7E8, 0xD4CA64EB,
        0x8AD55E3E, 0x78BEE structure, 0x6BE02EC9, 0x998BA structure, 0x4D4FC921, 0xBF244A22, 0xAC74B9D6, 0x5E1F3AD5
    };
    for (size_t i = 0; i < length; ++i) {
        crc = (crc >> 8) ^ table[(crc ^ data[i]) & 0xFF];
    }
    return crc;
#endif
}

// ============================================================================
// 2. Lock-Free Epoch-Based Memory Reclamation (EBR) Subsystem
// ============================================================================
class EpochManager {
public:
    static constexpr size_t NUM_EPOCHS = 3;
    static constexpr size_t MAX_THREADS = 128;
    static constexpr size_t RETIRE_BATCH_THRESHOLD = 64;

    struct alignas(64) ThreadDescriptor {
        std::atomic<uint64_t> active_epoch{INACTIVE_EPOCH};
        std::atomic<bool> in_use{false};
        std::array<std::vector<void (*)(void*)>, NUM_EPOCHS> retire_callbacks;
        std::array<std::vector<void*>, NUM_EPOCHS> retire_pointers;
        uint64_t local_ops_count{0};
    };

    static constexpr uint64_t INACTIVE_EPOCH = std::numeric_limits<uint64_t>::max();

private:
    std::atomic<uint64_t> global_epoch_{0};
    std::array<ThreadDescriptor, MAX_THREADS> threads_;
    std::atomic<size_t> num_registered_threads_{0};

    EpochManager() = default;

public:
    static EpochManager& Instance() {
        static EpochManager instance;
        return instance;
    }

    size_t RegisterThread() {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < MAX_THREADS; ++i) {
            bool expected = false;
            if (threads_[i].in_use.compare_exchange_strong(expected, true, std::memory_order_acq_rel)) {
                num_registered_threads_.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
                return i;
            }
        }
        throw std::runtime_error("Maximum registered threads exceeded in EBR");
    }

    void DeregisterThread(size_t tid) {
        assert(tid < MAX_THREADS);
        FlushRetireQueue(tid, true);
        threads_[tid].active_epoch.store(INACTIVE_EPOCH, std::memory_order_release);
        threads_[tid].in_use.store(false, std::memory_order_release);
        num_registered_threads_.fetch_sub(1, std::memory_order_relaxed);
    }

    void EnterCriticalSection(size_t tid) {
        uint64_t cur_epoch = global_epoch_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
        threads_[tid].active_epoch.store(cur_epoch, std::memory_order_release);
        std::atomic_thread_fence(std::memory_order_seq_cst);
    }

    void LeaveCriticalSection(size_t tid) {
        threads_[tid].active_epoch.store(INACTIVE_EPOCH, std::memory_order_release);
        threads_[tid].local_ops_count++;
        if (threads_[tid].local_ops_count % RETIRE_BATCH_THRESHOLD == 0) {
            TryAdvanceAndReclaim(tid);
        }
    }

    template <typename T>
    void Retire(size_t tid, T* ptr) {
        if (!ptr) return;
        uint64_t cur_epoch = global_epoch_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) % NUM_EPOCHS;
        threads_[tid].retire_pointers[cur_epoch].push_back(ptr);
        threads_[tid].retire_callbacks[cur_epoch].push_back([](void* p) {
            delete static_cast<T*>(p);
        });

        if (threads_[tid].retire_pointers[cur_epoch].size() >= RETIRE_BATCH_THRESHOLD) {
            TryAdvanceAndReclaim(tid);
        }
    }

    void TryAdvanceAndReclaim(size_t tid) {
        uint64_t cur_epoch = global_epoch_.load(std::memory_order_acquire);

        // Quiescent verification: can we advance epoch?
        bool can_advance = true;
        for (size_t i = 0; i < MAX_THREADS; ++i) {
            if (!threads_[i].in_use.load(std::memory_order_relaxed)) continue;
            uint64_t th_epoch = threads_[i].active_epoch.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
            if (th_epoch != INACTIVE_EPOCH && th_epoch != cur_epoch) {
                can_advance = false;
                break;
            }
        }

        if (can_advance) {
            if (global_epoch_.compare_exchange_strong(cur_epoch, cur_epoch + 1, std::memory_order_acq_rel)) {
                cur_epoch++;
            }
        }

        // Reclaim buffers from (cur_epoch + 1) % NUM_EPOCHS which is guaranteed unreferenced
        size_t reclaim_epoch = (cur_epoch + 1) % NUM_EPOCHS;
        auto& ptrs = threads_[tid].retire_pointers[reclaim_epoch];
        auto& cbs = threads_[tid].retire_callbacks[reclaim_epoch];

        for (size_t i = 0; i < ptrs.size(); ++i) {
            cbs[i](ptrs[i]);
        }
        ptrs.clear();
        cbs.clear();
    }

    void FlushRetireQueue(size_t tid, bool force_all = false) {
        for (size_t e = 0; e < NUM_EPOCHS; ++e) {
            if (force_all) {
                auto& ptrs = threads_[tid].retire_pointers[e];
                auto& cbs = threads_[tid].retire_callbacks[e];
                for (size_t i = 0; i < ptrs.size(); ++i) {
                    cbs[i](ptrs[i]);
                }
                ptrs.clear();
                cbs.clear();
            }
        }
    }
};

struct EpochGuard {
    size_t thread_id;
    EpochGuard(size_t tid) : thread_id(tid) {
        EpochManager::Instance().EnterCriticalSection(thread_id);
    }
    ~EpochGuard() {
        EpochManager::Instance().LeaveCriticalSection(thread_id);
    }
    EpochGuard(const EpochGuard&) = delete;
    EpochGuard& operator=(const EpochGuard&) = delete;
};

// ============================================================================
// 3. Tagged Pointer Abstraction for Lock-Free SkipList
// ============================================================================
template <typename T>
class MarkedPtr {
private:
    uintptr_t ptr_{0};
    static constexpr uintptr_t MARK_MASK = 0x1;

public:
    constexpr MarkedPtr() noexcept : ptr_(0) {}
    constexpr MarkedPtr(T* ptr, bool mark = false) noexcept 
        : ptr_(reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(ptr) | (mark ? MARK_MASK : 0)) {}

    T* Get(bool& is_marked) const noexcept {
        is_marked = (ptr_ & MARK_MASK) != 0;
        return reinterpret_cast<T*>(ptr_ & ~MARK_MASK);
    }

    T* GetPtr() const noexcept {
        return reinterpret_cast<T*>(ptr_ & ~MARK_MASK);
    }

    bool IsMarked() const noexcept {
        return (ptr_ & MARK_MASK) != 0;
    }

    uintptr_t Raw() const noexcept { return ptr_; }
};

// ============================================================================
// 4. Lock-Free MVCC SkipList Data Structures
// ============================================================================
using TxTimestamp = uint64_t;

struct VersionNode {
    TxTimestamp commit_ts;
    bool is_tombstone;
    std::string value;
    std::atomic<VersionNode*> next{nullptr};

    VersionNode(TxTimestamp ts, bool tombstone, std::string_view val)
        : commit_ts(ts), is_tombstone(tombstone), value(val), next(nullptr) {}
};

template <typename Key>
struct SkipListNode {
    Key key;
    size_t height;
    std::atomic<VersionNode*> head_version{nullptr};
    std::atomic<MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>> next[1];

    static SkipListNode* Create(const Key& k, size_t height, VersionNode* initial_version) {
        size_t alloc_size = sizeof(SkipListNode) + sizeof(std::atomic<MarkedPtr<SkipListNode>>) * (height > 0 ? height - 1 : 0);
        void* mem = ::operator new(alloc_size);
        return new (mem) SkipListNode(k, height, initial_version);
    }

    static void Destroy(SkipListNode* node) {
        if (!node) return;
        // Drain MVCC versions
        VersionNode* v = node->head_version.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
        while (v) {
            VersionNode* nv = v->next.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
            delete v;
            v = nv;
        }
        node->~SkipListNode();
        ::operator delete(node);
    }

private:
    SkipListNode(const Key& k, size_t h, VersionNode* initial_version)
        : key(k), height(h), head_version(initial_version) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < height; ++i) {
            next[i].store(MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>(nullptr, false), std::memory_order_relaxed);
        }
    }
};

// ============================================================================
// 5. Lock-Free MVCC SkipList Engine
// ============================================================================
template <typename Key, typename Compare = std::less<Key>>
class ConcurrentSkipListMap {
public:
    static constexpr size_t MAX_LEVEL = 32;
    static constexpr float PROBABILITY = 0.5f;

private:
    Compare comp_;
    SkipListNode<Key>* head_;
    SkipListNode<Key>* tail_;
    std::atomic<size_t> max_height_{1};

    size_t RandomHeight(size_t tid) {
        static thread_local std::mt19937_64 generator(1337 + tid * 7919);
        static thread_local std::geometric_distribution<size_t> distribution(PROBABILITY);
        size_t h = distribution(generator) + 1;
        return std::min(h, MAX_LEVEL);
    }

public:
    ConcurrentSkipListMap() {
        head_ = SkipListNode<Key>::Create(Key(), MAX_LEVEL, nullptr);
        tail_ = SkipListNode<Key>::Create(Key(), MAX_LEVEL, nullptr);
        for (size_t i = 0; i < MAX_LEVEL; ++i) {
            head_->next[i].store(MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>(tail_, false), std::memory_order_relaxed);
            tail_->next[i].store(MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>(nullptr, false), std::memory_order_relaxed);
        }
    }

    ~ConcurrentSkipListMap() {
        SkipListNode<Key>* curr = head_->next[0].load(std::memory_order_relaxed).GetPtr();
        while (curr != tail_ && curr != nullptr) {
            SkipListNode<Key>* next = curr->next[0].load(std::memory_order_relaxed).GetPtr();
            SkipListNode<Key>::Destroy(curr);
            curr = next;
        }
        SkipListNode<Key>::Destroy(head_);
        SkipListNode<Key>::Destroy(tail_);
    }

    // Search helper that performs physical unlinking of marked nodes
    bool Find(const Key& key, 
              std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL>& preds, 
              std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL>& succs, 
              size_t tid) {
        bool retry = true;
        while (retry) {
            retry = false;
            SkipListNode<Key>* pred = head_;
            for (int level = static_cast<int>(MAX_LEVEL) - 1; level >= 0; --level) {
                SkipListNode<Key>* curr = pred->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire).GetPtr();
                while (true) {
                    if (curr == tail_) {
                        break;
                    }
                    bool is_marked = false;
                    MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> succ = curr->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire);
                    SkipListNode<Key>* succ_ptr = succ.Get(is_marked);

                    while (is_marked) {
                        // Cooperative physical unlink via CAS
                        MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> expected(curr, false);
                        MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> desired(succ_ptr, false);
                        if (!pred->next[level].compare_exchange_weak(expected, desired,
                                                                     std::memory_order_acq_rel, 
                                                                     std::memory_order_acquire)) {
                            retry = true;
                            break;
                        }
                        // Queue the node for reclamation when level 0 is unlinked
                        if (level == 0) {
                            EpochManager::Instance().Retire(tid, curr);
                        }
                        curr = succ_ptr;
                        if (curr == tail_) break;
                        succ = curr->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire);
                        succ_ptr = succ.Get(is_marked);
                    }
                    if (retry) break;

                    if (curr != tail_ && comp_(curr->key, key)) {
                        pred = curr;
                        curr = succ_ptr;
                    } else {
                        break;
                    }
                }
                if (retry) break;
                preds[level] = pred;
                succs[level] = curr;
            }
            if (!retry) {
                return (succs[0] != tail_ && !comp_(key, succs[0]->key) && !comp_(succs[0]->key, key));
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    bool Insert(const Key& key, std::string_view value, TxTimestamp commit_ts, size_t tid) {
        EpochGuard guard(tid);
        std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL> preds;
        std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL> succs;

        while (true) {
            bool found = Find(key, preds, succs, tid);
            if (found) {
                // Key exists: atomically prepend new MVCC version to the node
                SkipListNode<Key>* node = succs[0];
                auto* new_version = new VersionNode(commit_ts, false, value);
                VersionNode* cur_head = node->head_version.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
                while (true) {
                    new_version->next.store(cur_head, std::memory_order_relaxed);
                    if (node->head_version.compare_exchange_weak(cur_head, new_version, 
                                                                 std::memory_order_release, 
                                                                 std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
                        return true;
                    }
                }
            }

            // Key does not exist: create and splice new node
            size_t height = RandomHeight(tid);
            auto* initial_version = new VersionNode(commit_ts, false, value);
            SkipListNode<Key>* new_node = SkipListNode<Key>::Create(key, height, initial_version);

            for (size_t i = 0; i < height; ++i) {
                new_node->next[i].store(MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>(succs[i], false), std::memory_order_relaxed);
            }

            MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> expected(succs[0], false);
            MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> desired(new_node, false);
            if (!preds[0]->next[0].compare_exchange_strong(expected, desired, 
                                                           std::memory_order_acq_rel, 
                                                           std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
                // Splicing level 0 failed: deallocate new_node and retry
                SkipListNode<Key>::Destroy(new_node);
                continue;
            }

            // Splice higher levels
            for (size_t i = 1; i < height; ++i) {
                while (true) {
                    MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> exp(succs[i], false);
                    MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> des(new_node, false);
                    if (preds[i]->next[i].compare_exchange_weak(exp, des, 
                                                                std::memory_order_acq_rel, 
                                                                std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
                        break;
                    }
                    // Re-evaluate predecessors if CAS fails
                    Find(key, preds, succs, tid);
                    new_node->next[i].store(MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>>(succs[i], false), std::memory_order_relaxed);
                }
            }
            return true;
        }
    }

    bool Delete(const Key& key, TxTimestamp commit_ts, size_t tid) {
        EpochGuard guard(tid);
        std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL> preds;
        std::array<SkipListNode<Key>*, MAX_LEVEL> succs;

        while (true) {
            bool found = Find(key, preds, succs, tid);
            if (!found) {
                return false;
            }

            SkipListNode<Key>* node_to_delete = succs[0];
            // MVCC logical tombstone version prepend
            auto* tombstone = new VersionNode(commit_ts, true, "");
            VersionNode* cur_head = node_to_delete->head_version.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
            while (true) {
                tombstone->next.store(cur_head, std::memory_order_relaxed);
                if (node_to_delete->head_version.compare_exchange_weak(cur_head, tombstone, 
                                                                       std::memory_order_release, 
                                                                       std::memory_order_relaxed)) {
                    break;
                }
            }

            // Physically mark levels from top to bottom
            for (int level = static_cast<int>(node_to_delete->height) - 1; level >= 0; --level) {
                while (true) {
                    MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> succ = node_to_delete->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire);
                    if (succ.IsMarked()) break;
                    MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> marked_succ(succ.GetPtr(), true);
                    if (node_to_delete->next[level].compare_exchange_weak(succ, marked_succ, 
                                                                          std::memory_order_acq_rel, 
                                                                          std::memory_order_acquire)) {
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
            // Trigger physical removal
            Find(key, preds, succs, tid);
            return true;
        }
    }

    std::optional<std::string> Get(const Key& key, TxTimestamp read_ts, size_t tid) {
        EpochGuard guard(tid);
        SkipListNode<Key>* pred = head_;
        SkipListNode<Key>* curr = nullptr;

        for (int level = static_cast<int>(MAX_LEVEL) - 1; level >= 0; --level) {
            curr = pred->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire).GetPtr();
            while (true) {
                if (curr == tail_) break;
                MarkedPtr<SkipListNode<Key>> succ = curr->next[level].load(std::memory_order_acquire);
                if (curr != tail_ && comp_(curr->key, key)) {
                    pred = curr;
                    curr = succ.GetPtr();
                } else {
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        if (curr != tail_ && !comp_(key, curr->key) && !comp_(curr->key, key)) {
            // Traverse MVCC version chain (Wait-Free)
            VersionNode* version = curr->head_version.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
            while (version != nullptr) {
                if (version->commit_ts <= read_ts) {
                    if (version->is_tombstone) {
                        return std::nullopt;
                    }
                    return version->value;
                }
                version = version->next.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
            }
        }
        return std::nullopt;
    }
};

// ============================================================================
// 6. Zero-Copy io_uring Group-Commit WAL Subsystem
// ============================================================================
#pragma pack(push, 1)
struct WALRecordHeader {
    uint32_t crc32c;
    uint8_t  record_type; // 1: Insert/Update, 2: Delete
    uint64_t tx_id;
    uint64_t commit_ts;
    uint32_t key_len;
    uint32_t value_len;
    uint64_t prev_lsn;
};
#pragma pack(pop)

struct WALTask {
    WALRecordHeader header;
    std::string key;
    std::string value;
    std::atomic<bool> is_persisted{false};
    WALTask* next{nullptr};
};

// Lock-Free Single-Consumer MPSC Queue for WAL submission
class LockFreeMPSCQueue {
private:
    struct alignas(64) Node {
        std::atomic<Node*> next{nullptr};
        WALTask* task{nullptr};
    };
    alignas(64) std::atomic<Node*> head_;
    alignas(64) Node* tail_;
    Node* stub_;

public:
    LockFreeMPSCQueue() {
        stub_ = new Node();
        head_.store(stub_, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        tail_ = stub_;
    }

    ~LockFreeMPSCQueue() {
        while (WALTask* t = Pop()) {
            delete t;
        }
        delete stub_;
    }

    void Push(WALTask* task) {
        auto* n = new Node();
        n->task = task;
        n->next.store(nullptr, std::memory_order_relaxed);
        Node* prev = head_.exchange(n, std::memory_order_acq_rel);
        prev->next.store(n, std::memory_order_release);
    }

    WALTask* Pop() {
        Node* tail = tail_;
        Node* next = tail->next.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
        if (next != nullptr) {
            tail_ = next;
            WALTask* task = next->task;
            delete tail;
            return task;
        }
        return nullptr;
    }
};

class AsyncWALCommitter {
public:
    static constexpr size_t RING_ENTRIES = 1024;
    static constexpr size_t BUFFER_SIZE = 4 * 1024 * 1024; // 4MB Committer page
    static constexpr size_t BATCH_FLUSH_BYTES = 64 * 1024; // 64KB threshold
    static constexpr uint64_t FLUSH_TIMEOUT_US = 50;

private:
    int fd_{-1};
    struct io_uring ring_;
    LockFreeMPSCQueue queue_;
    std::atomic<bool> running_{false};
    std::thread committer_thread_;
    std::atomic<uint64_t> current_lsn_{0};

    // Registered fixed buffer
    alignas(4096) uint8_t buffer_[BUFFER_SIZE];
    struct iovec iov_;

    void CommitterLoop() {
        std::vector<WALTask*> current_batch;
        current_batch.reserve(2048);
        size_t buffer_offset = 0;
        uint64_t file_offset = 0;

        auto last_flush_time = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();

        while (running_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed) || queue_.Pop() != nullptr) {
            WALTask* task = nullptr;
            while ((task = queue_.Pop()) != nullptr) {
                // Serialize into buffer
                size_t record_len = sizeof(WALRecordHeader) + task->header.key_len + task->header.value_len;
                if (buffer_offset + record_len > BUFFER_SIZE) {
                    FlushBuffer(buffer_offset, file_offset, current_batch);
                    file_offset += buffer_offset;
                    buffer_offset = 0;
                }

                // Compute CRC
                task->header.prev_lsn = current_lsn_.load(std::memory_order_relaxed);
                uint8_t* dest = buffer_ + buffer_offset;
                std::memcpy(dest, &task->header, sizeof(WALRecordHeader));
                std::memcpy(dest + sizeof(WALRecordHeader), task->key.data(), task->header.key_len);
                std::memcpy(dest + sizeof(WALRecordHeader) + task->header.key_len, task->value.data(), task->header.value_len);

                // Checksum calculated over payload + metadata
                uint32_t crc = calculate_crc32c(0, dest + sizeof(uint32_t), record_len - sizeof(uint32_t));
                reinterpret_cast<WALRecordHeader*>(dest)->crc32c = crc;

                buffer_offset += record_len;
                current_lsn_.fetch_add(record_len, std::memory_order_relaxed);
                current_batch.push_back(task);

                if (buffer_offset >= BATCH_FLUSH_BYTES) {
                    break;
                }
            }

            auto now = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
            auto elapsed_us = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::microseconds>(now - last_flush_time).count();

            if (buffer_offset > 0 && (buffer_offset >= BATCH_FLUSH_BYTES || elapsed_us >= FLUSH_TIMEOUT_US)) {
                FlushBuffer(buffer_offset, file_offset, current_batch);
                file_offset += buffer_offset;
                buffer_offset = 0;
                last_flush_time = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
            } else if (buffer_offset == 0) {
                std::this_thread::yield();
            }
        }

        if (buffer_offset > 0) {
            FlushBuffer(buffer_offset, file_offset, current_batch);
        }
    }

    void FlushBuffer(size_t size, uint64_t file_offset, std::vector<WALTask*>& batch) {
        if (size == 0) return;

        // Vectorized io_uring write
        struct io_uring_sqe* sqe = io_uring_get_sqe(&ring_);
        io_uring_prep_write_fixed(sqe, fd_, buffer_, size, file_offset, 0);
        sqe->flags |= IOSQE_IO_LINK;

        // Linked fsync
        struct io_uring_sqe* sqe_fsync = io_uring_get_sqe(&ring_);
        io_uring_prep_fsync(sqe_fsync, fd_, IORING_FSYNC_DATASYNC);
        io_uring_sqe_set_data(sqe_fsync, reinterpret_cast<void*>(1));

        io_uring_submit_and_wait(&ring_, 2);

        // Reap completions
        struct io_uring_cqe* cqe;
        unsigned head;
        unsigned count = 0;
        io_uring_for_each_cqe(&ring_, head, cqe) {
            count++;
        }
        io_uring_cq_advance(&ring_, count);

        // Notify waiting threads
        for (auto* task : batch) {
            task->is_persisted.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
        }
        batch.clear();
    }

public:
    AsyncWALCommitter(const std::string& path) {
        fd_ = open(path.c_str(), O_CREAT | O_RDWR | O_DIRECT | O_TRUNC, 0644);
        if (fd_ < 0) {
            // Fallback without O_DIRECT if filesystem does not support it
            fd_ = open(path.c_str(), O_CREAT | O_RDWR | O_TRUNC, 0644);
            if (fd_ < 0) throw std::system_error(errno, std::generic_category(), "Failed to open WAL file");
        }

        struct io_uring_params params;
        std::memset(&params, 0, sizeof(params));
        if (io_uring_queue_init_params(RING_ENTRIES, &ring_, &params) < 0) {
            throw std::runtime_error("io_uring_queue_init failed");
        }

        iov_.iov_base = buffer_;
        iov_.iov_len = BUFFER_SIZE;
        if (io_uring_register_buffers(&ring_, &iov_, 1) < 0) {
            throw std::runtime_error("io_uring_register_buffers failed");
        }

        running_.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
        committer_thread_ = std::thread(&AsyncWALCommitter::CommitterLoop, this);
    }

    ~AsyncWALCommitter() {
        running_.store(false, std::memory_order_release);
        if (committer_thread_.joinable()) {
            committer_thread_.join();
        }
        io_uring_unregister_buffers(&ring_);
        io_uring_queue_exit(&ring_);
        if (fd_ >= 0) close(fd_);
    }

    void Append(uint8_t type, uint64_t tx_id, uint64_t commit_ts, std::string_view key, std::string_view value) {
        auto* task = new WALTask();
        task->header.record_type = type;
        task->header.tx_id = tx_id;
        task->header.commit_ts = commit_ts;
        task->header.key_len = static_cast<uint32_t>(key.size());
        task->header.value_len = static_cast<uint32_t>(value.size());
        task->key = key;
        task->value = value;

        queue_.Push(task);

        // Spin-wait / Exponential backoff for group durability completion
        uint32_t spin_count = 0;
        while (!task->is_persisted.load(std::memory_order_acquire)) {
            if (spin_count++ < 1000) {
                #if defined(__x86_64__) || defined(_M_X64)
                _mm_pause();
                #endif
            } else {
                std::this_thread::yield();
            }
        }
        delete task;
    }
};

// ============================================================================
// 7. Transactional Storage Engine Interface
// ============================================================================
class MVCCStorageEngine {
private:
    ConcurrentSkipListMap<std::string> index_;
    std::unique_ptr<AsyncWALCommitter> wal_;
    std::atomic<TxTimestamp> global_ts_{1};

public:
    MVCCStorageEngine(const std::string& wal_path) {
        wal_ = std::make_unique<AsyncWALCommitter>(wal_path);
    }

    TxTimestamp BeginTransaction() {
        return global_ts_.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
    }

    bool Put(std::string_view key, std::string_view value, size_t tid) {
        TxTimestamp ts = global_ts_.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_acq_rel);
        wal_->Append(1, ts, ts, key, value);
        return index_.Insert(std::string(key), value, ts, tid);
    }

    bool Delete(std::string_view key, size_t tid) {
        TxTimestamp ts = global_ts_.fetch_add(1, std::memory_order_acq_rel);
        wal_->Append(2, ts, ts, key, "");
        return index_.Delete(std::string(key), ts, tid);
    }

    std::optional<std::string> Get(std::string_view key, TxTimestamp read_ts, size_t tid) {
        return index_.Get(std::string(key), read_ts, tid);
    }

    // Deterministic crash recovery and rebuild procedure
    static void Recover(const std::string& wal_path, ConcurrentSkipListMap<std::string>& target_index, size_t tid) {
        int fd = open(wal_path.c_str(), O_RDONLY);
        if (fd < 0) return;

        struct stat st;
        fstat(fd, &st);
        size_t file_size = st.st_size;
        std::vector<uint8_t> buffer(file_size);
        ssize_t read_bytes = read(fd, buffer.data(), file_size);
        close(fd);

        if (read_bytes <= 0) return;

        size_t offset = 0;
        uint64_t valid_records = 0;

        while (offset + sizeof(WALRecordHeader) <= static_cast<size_t>(read_bytes)) {
            const auto* hdr = reinterpret_cast<const WALRecordHeader*>(buffer.data() + offset);
            size_t record_len = sizeof(WALRecordHeader) + hdr->key_len + hdr->value_len;

            if (offset + record_len > static_cast<size_t>(read_bytes)) {
                // Partial / torn write detected at end of log
                break;
            }

            // Verify checksum
            uint32_t computed_crc = calculate_crc32c(0, buffer.data() + offset + sizeof(uint32_t), record_len - sizeof(uint32_t));
            if (computed_crc != hdr->crc32c) {
                // Corrupted record encountered; stop replay
                break;
            }

            std::string_view k(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(buffer.data() + offset + sizeof(WALRecordHeader)), hdr->key_len);
            std::string_view v(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(buffer.data() + offset + sizeof(WALRecordHeader) + hdr->key_len), hdr->value_len);

            if (hdr->record_type == 1) {
                target_index.Insert(std::string(k), v, hdr->commit_ts, tid);
            } else if (hdr->record_type == 2) {
                target_index.Delete(std::string(k), hdr->commit_ts, tid);
            }

            offset += record_len;
            valid_records++;
        }
        std::cout << "[Recovery] Successfully replayed " << valid_records << " mutations from WAL.\n";
    }
};

} // namespace mvcc

#endif // MVCC_STORAGE_ENGINE_HPP
